The prompt-assembly structure follows Codex: the per-model instructions template
with a personality slot, the sandbox_mode x approval_policy permissions matrix,
the guardian policy, the compaction handoff pair, and the agent role file
(the swarm member's). Open Math OS modified the
files: their text is rewritten for this system's tools and services, which
differ from Codex's, and some of Codex's wording remains. The
notice and Codex's license text are in ../third-party/NOTICES.txt and
../LICENSE, and the VM runtime package carries both.

One thing is deliberately NOT copied in substance. In Codex the guardian
classifier and the permissions prose are how command safety is decided,
because Codex has no kernel underneath. Here there is no classifier, and the
guardian policy and the permissions prose are description only: the
tools an agent may call are derived by the kernel from the capabilities it
holds, and approval is the `approvals` service with its own boundary. If a
guardian template and the capability set ever disagree, the capability set is
what happens.
